1
00:00:00,899 --> 00:00:05,500
T

2
00:01:16,449 --> 00:01:18,749
About a billion years ago...

3
00:01:18,749 --> 00:01:20,499
During the Cretaceous Period,

4
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:23,700
The Earth was ruled by Reptiles.

5
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:27,150
Among them, the one suitably labeled King,

6
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:29,300
Was this Tyrannosaurus Rex.

7
00:01:30,499 --> 00:01:31,349
Wow. This is...

8
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:32,900
A fragment of a Dinosaur?

9
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:34,499
Is this real?

10
00:01:34,499 --> 00:01:35,749
Of course it is.

11
00:01:36,099 --> 00:01:38,999
It was found in the National Park in Utah.

12
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,250
It's a present from my Dad's trip to America.

13
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:43,499
Well, well...

14
00:01:43,499 --> 00:01:44,649
Let me have a closer look.

15
00:01:44,650 --> 00:01:45,400
Hey, hang on!

16
00:01:47,099 --> 00:01:51,099
So this was living and moving
around a billion years ago?

17
00:01:51,099 --> 00:01:53,249
Hey, let me have a look too.

18
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:55,500
Here, Shizuka-chan, take a closer look at it.

19
00:01:56,900 --> 00:02:01,650
When I stare at it like this, it's as if
I can see a picture of that period.

20
00:02:02,099 --> 00:02:04,549
With the densely overgrown fern forests,

21
00:02:04,549 --> 00:02:06,499
And Dinosaurs the size of hills.

22
00:02:06,499 --> 00:02:09,798
Come on. Hurry and let me have a look too.

23
00:02:09,798 --> 00:02:11,198
Okay, okay. That's enough.

24
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:12,949
I'm going to put it away.

25
00:02:12,949 --> 00:02:14,949
I don't want it to get broken.

26
00:02:18,699 --> 00:02:19,599
Geez...

27
00:02:20,899 --> 00:02:23,299
Suneo-kun, thank you for showing
us something so precious.

28
00:02:23,299 --> 00:02:25,848
If you want to see it again, stop by anytime.

29
00:02:25,848 --> 00:02:28,698
Da Hell! Don't brag because of a mere fossil.

30
00:02:28,699 --> 00:02:29,649
Huh??

31
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,000
I will declare this here.

32
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,449
I won't just find a fossil of a claw, but
I will find an entire Dinosaur fossil!

33
00:02:37,598 --> 00:02:38,698
Oops.

34
00:02:38,699 --> 00:02:40,899
I said something I shouldn't have once again.

35
00:02:41,598 --> 00:02:43,948
What?! You making stuff up again?

36
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:45,299
I'm not lying!

37
00:02:45,299 --> 00:02:48,399
If I am, I'll eat spaghetti through my nose!

38
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:54,849
Uh-oh, I have a bad habit of spouting
nonsense when I'm vexed.

39
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,300
Now I absolutely have to find a Dinosaur fossil

40
00:03:07,349 --> 00:03:09,150
And a whole one no less.

41
00:03:09,699 --> 00:03:10,399
EH?!

42
00:03:10,598 --> 00:03:12,848
A whole Dinosaur fossil??!

43
00:03:12,848 --> 00:03:14,048
Doraemon, please.

44
00:03:14,299 --> 00:03:18,149
You need to think about where it's possible
or not before you say things.

45
00:03:18,149 --> 00:03:20,549
Doraemon, you're the only
one that can help me...

46
00:03:20,550 --> 00:03:21,600
Pleeease.

47
00:03:21,899 --> 00:03:22,449
Ne?

48
00:03:23,149 --> 00:03:24,999
Listen up, Nobita-kun.

49
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,149
Japan never had any Tyrranosauruses here.

50
00:03:29,149 --> 00:03:29,899
Eh?

51
00:03:30,848 --> 00:03:34,899
How do you propose I produce
a non-existant Dinosaur fossil?

52
00:03:35,299 --> 00:03:36,899
Can't you do something?

53
00:03:36,899 --> 00:03:37,549
I'm telling you...

54
00:03:37,899 --> 00:03:40,798
You're so irresponsible,

55
00:03:40,798 --> 00:03:42,448
Or rather inconsiderate,

56
00:03:42,449 --> 00:03:44,349
Or rather incompetent...

57
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:45,750
Enough!!

58
00:03:46,550 --> 00:03:47,950
I can't back down now.

59
00:03:48,299 --> 00:03:50,449
H'll do it myself, so don't bother!

60
00:04:03,848 --> 00:04:06,048
I wonder where he gathered all that from...

61
00:04:08,349 --> 00:04:11,699
But with that brain of his, I doubt
that he understands half of it.

62
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,149
I'm sure he'll probably get bored
and quit pretty quickly.

63
00:04:14,149 --> 00:04:17,099
It's commendable that he tries to
work things out on his own,

64
00:04:17,649 --> 00:04:21,598
It doesn't matter if he screws up.
I'll kindly watch over him.

65
00:04:27,699 --> 00:04:28,949
What do you want?

66
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:31,300
I'm trying to show you my
kindly watching over.

67
00:04:33,449 --> 00:04:36,199
Don't bother me by looking
at me with that dopey grin.

68
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,500
Hmph!

69
00:04:40,399 --> 00:04:41,199
What is this?

70
00:04:41,199 --> 00:04:43,399
Fossils are located in the oldest
Geological Stratum.

71
00:04:43,399 --> 00:04:49,399
Stratum can be seen as layers of dirt
revealed by Earthquakes or mining

72
00:04:49,399 --> 00:04:50,899
Oh, I see...

73
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,899
My instinct tells me this is the ideal spot.
T

74
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:10,050
I thought I'd find something...

75
00:05:10,050 --> 00:05:12,298
But I guess I was off.

76
00:05:12,298 --> 00:05:13,298
HEY YOU!!

77
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:17,150
What are you doing up there?

78
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:24,100
What were you doing up there?

79
00:05:24,850 --> 00:05:25,699
I'm sorry.

80
00:05:25,699 --> 00:05:28,249
I was just about to quit, so don't worry.

81
00:05:28,250 --> 00:05:30,250
It's not about you quitting

82
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:30,600
Take a look.

83
00:05:35,850 --> 00:05:38,199
Eh? I did all that?

84
00:05:38,199 --> 00:05:39,849
Yeah, you did. What are you
going to do about it?

85
00:05:39,850 --> 00:05:41,500
What should I do?

86
00:05:41,699 --> 00:05:42,299
Let's see...

87
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:45,149
Then, dig me a hole for my rubbish.

88
00:05:45,298 --> 00:05:46,548
More digging?

89
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:55,850
Of all the things... have to do this. It's
all because Doraemon refused to help.

90
00:05:58,850 --> 00:05:59,400
Huh?

91
00:06:03,298 --> 00:06:04,848
It's a Dinosaur egg!!

92
00:06:05,298 --> 00:06:06,149
YAAAYYY!!!

93
00:06:06,149 --> 00:06:09,049
I finally found it!

94
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:16,348
I did it! I did it! I did it!

95
00:06:16,348 --> 00:06:17,798
Hey you! Wait!!

96
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:20,899
Doraemon!

97
00:06:35,899 --> 00:06:37,250
It's a Dinosaur egg

98
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:40,298
Look! Look! How about it?
I found this all by myself.

99
00:06:40,298 --> 00:06:41,348
Are you proud of me?

100
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:46,449
But, how do you know that
this is a Dinosaur egg?

101
00:06:47,899 --> 00:06:50,348
It might be just a rock,

102
00:06:50,348 --> 00:06:54,548
And even if it were a fossil, it could
be a Prehistoric seed or something.

103
00:06:55,699 --> 00:06:58,949
Or it could be a Mammoth Dung.

104
00:06:59,399 --> 00:07:00,598
Dung?

105
00:07:00,598 --> 00:07:01,498
Yeah, that's right.

106
00:07:02,199 --> 00:07:03,899
Well, you don't know what it is, right?

107
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:06,800
Don't say such things.

108
00:07:09,850 --> 00:07:13,050
Even so, there's no way to
know for sure what it is.

109
00:07:13,050 --> 00:07:15,850
What should do, Doraemon?!

110
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:23,649
I remember using it before.

111
00:07:23,649 --> 00:07:27,499
Anything wrapped in this will go back in time.

112
00:07:44,899 --> 00:07:48,699
If I make this fossil go back in time
a billion years just like this,

113
00:07:48,699 --> 00:07:50,699
Then we'll find out its true identity for sure.

114
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:51,750
Yes.

115
00:07:51,750 --> 00:07:53,149
That's the right thing to do.

116
00:07:53,149 --> 00:07:56,799
Lately, it seems you've developed a
habit of relying on me too much.

117
00:07:56,800 --> 00:08:00,500
If it continues, then you'll never
develop independence.

118
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:05,199
I hope that you will think for yourself, and
solve problems using your own strengths.

119
00:08:05,199 --> 00:08:09,699
I will quietly and gently watch over you, okay?

120
00:08:09,699 --> 00:08:11,299
This is taking a while.

121
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:16,300
Of course, it DOES have to
go back a billion years...

122
00:08:18,649 --> 00:08:19,098
Huh?

123
00:08:27,050 --> 00:08:27,899
Yay!

124
00:08:27,899 --> 00:08:29,199
There's no mistake, it's an egg!

125
00:08:29,199 --> 00:08:30,000
Yoshin

126
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
I'm gonna hatch it!

127
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:37,600
Oh my.

128
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:40,500
What are you doing? It's still midday.

129
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:43,200
If you want to send someone to
the store, have Doraemon go.

130
00:08:43,499 --> 00:08:45,548
I'm busy right now.

131
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,100
No! Let go!

132
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:50,499
Hey, Nobita!

133
00:08:50,499 --> 00:08:51,349
Come on!

134
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:53,700
Such a troublesome kid.

135
00:09:04,299 --> 00:09:06,899
Papa, please do something

136
00:09:07,449 --> 00:09:10,499
Nobita's been sleeping while it's still midday.

137
00:09:11,349 --> 00:09:12,299
Nobita!

138
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:22,300
What's going on?

139
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:24,050
Oh no...wait

140
00:09:24,050 --> 00:09:26,050
It's that...come over here...

141
00:09:28,499 --> 00:09:31,449
He'll get over it soon, so let's leave him be.

142
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:41,600
Yoshi.

143
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,100
There's some hope.

144
00:09:43,349 --> 00:09:45,349
Just a bit more. I'm gonna try hard.

145
00:09:57,299 --> 00:09:58,349
Oh, no.

146
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:01,150
Doraemon!

147
00:10:01,150 --> 00:10:02,350
Wake up!

148
00:10:04,449 --> 00:10:06,149
Hey, hey, hey, hey. Hey!

149
00:10:06,399 --> 00:10:07,749
I said, hey!

150
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:11,700
I move around in my sleep,
and the egg is getting cold,

151
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:13,550
Could you tie me up with this?

152
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:19,399
Well, aren't you having it hard?

153
00:10:19,399 --> 00:10:20,599
Then...

154
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,300
Goodnight.

155
00:10:28,050 --> 00:10:28,800
Doraemon!

156
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:30,800
Untie me! Hurry!!

157
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:31,900
Hurry!

158
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:33,900
But I just tied you up.

159
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:37,100
Never mind that!! I'm about to pee my pants!!

160
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:06,700
It hatched!

161
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:16,500
There, there.

162
00:11:18,349 --> 00:11:19,749
Doraemon!

163
00:11:28,449 --> 00:11:29,799
Well, do you see?

164
00:11:31,499 --> 00:11:32,899
How about it?

165
00:11:33,250 --> 00:11:34,899
Try saying 'Guu

166
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,399
Well, I'm surprised.

167
00:11:38,399 --> 00:11:42,249
This is a Plesiosaur identified
as 'Futaba-Suzuki-Ryu'

168
00:11:42,548 --> 00:11:44,198
Futaba-Suzuki-Ryu?

169
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:44,750
Yeah.

170
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:48,900
It used to live in the waters near Japan
during the Cretaceous Period.

171
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:57,000
I wonder if he thinks I'm his parent?

172
00:11:57,250 --> 00:11:59,250
There, there. You're such a cutie.

173
00:11:59,250 --> 00:12:01,100
I will call you...

174
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:04,850
know!

175
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:06,000
It'll be 'P-suke!

176
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,450
I'll name you P-suke!

177
00:12:10,050 --> 00:12:13,449
Hey, let's call Suneo guys and surprise them.

178
00:12:13,449 --> 00:12:14,099
Wait.

179
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,299
That's where you're fast at jumping the gun.

180
00:12:16,299 --> 00:12:17,149
What?

181
00:12:17,499 --> 00:12:18,949
Think about it.

182
00:12:18,950 --> 00:12:23,299
What good will it do to show them something so small?
I know for sure they'll say it's a lizard and laugh at me.

183
00:12:23,299 --> 00:12:24,599
Besides that...

184
00:12:25,900 --> 00:12:28,100
Don't-don't tell me...

185
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:32,650
Yes, I'm gonna raise him. Till
he's at least ten meters.

186
00:12:32,650 --> 00:12:36,000
And let's shoot for the biggest
surprise when I reveal him.

187
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:40,950
I wonder what I should feed him.

188
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:42,950
No idea.

189
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,700
I guess I'll go get some worms.

190
00:12:57,700 --> 00:13:00,800
Lately, it's been hard to find earth worms.

191
00:13:02,399 --> 00:13:03,698
I'm not finding any.

192
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:05,900
Hey Nobita. Have you been practicing?

193
00:13:06,548 --> 00:13:07,899
Practicing what?

194
00:13:08,349 --> 00:13:10,749
Practicing eating spaghetti through your nose.

195
00:13:10,750 --> 00:13:11,250
Eh?

196
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:13,500
I'm looking forward to seeing it.

197
00:13:17,299 --> 00:13:20,849
Dare they mock me like that. Take this and this.

198
00:13:23,050 --> 00:13:24,499
Is the water hot enough?

199
00:13:24,499 --> 00:13:26,099
Yeah, it's just right.

200
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,548
Yes I did.
You heated the water?

201
00:13:27,548 --> 00:13:28,298
Yes I did.

202
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:31,400
P-suke!

203
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:32,449
What's going on?

204
00:13:32,449 --> 00:13:34,449
Mama, you're such a Dino-killer!!
What's going on?

205
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:35,650
P-suke!
The Time Furoshiki.

206
00:13:35,650 --> 00:13:36,800
Nobita-kun!
P-suke!

207
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:37,900
Doraemon!

208
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:40,100
Hey, hey, hey. Come over here.

209
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:43,499
P-suke! My P-suke...

210
00:13:43,499 --> 00:13:45,699
I moved him here.

211
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:51,550
Psuke

212
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,600
Here, P-suke.

213
00:13:57,399 --> 00:13:58,698
He won't eat.

214
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:01,050
Maybe he doesn't like earth worms.

215
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,548
What's the matter?

216
00:14:03,548 --> 00:14:05,899
Isn't Sashimi your favorite?

217
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:08,600
Yeah, I want to take my time
eating this in my room.

218
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,650
Me-me too.

219
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:17,300
Do you like it, Pasuke?

220
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:24,149
Eat plenty so you can grow big quickly.

221
00:14:25,050 --> 00:14:26,250
Nobita-kun,

222
00:14:26,250 --> 00:14:29,100
Instead of doing something so time consuming,

223
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:30,449
Why don't you give him this?

224
00:14:30,449 --> 00:14:31,349
What's that?

225
00:14:31,499 --> 00:14:33,548
Growth Acceleration Tablets.

226
00:14:33,548 --> 00:14:35,948
If you give him these, he'll grow better.

227
00:14:35,950 --> 00:14:37,750
Really? Thanks a lot.

228
00:14:54,349 --> 00:14:55,499
I'm home!

229
00:15:02,499 --> 00:15:03,798
P-suke!

230
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:05,349
Were you lonely?

231
00:15:05,349 --> 00:15:06,548
Now, let's play.

232
00:15:06,548 --> 00:15:07,649
There.

233
00:15:10,299 --> 00:15:11,299
Good. Good

234
00:15:11,299 --> 00:15:12,449
Here it goes.

235
00:15:12,449 --> 00:15:13,699
There

236
00:15:14,250 --> 00:15:16,049
Yoshi. One more.

237
00:15:16,299 --> 00:15:17,949
Here, that's good. Now over there.

238
00:15:19,399 --> 00:15:20,698
Nobita-kun,

239
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:25,299
Putting him in a cramped closet
day after day is bad for him,

240
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:27,799
Plus his play area is small too.

241
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:28,400
Yeah.

242
00:15:29,150 --> 00:15:31,700
Maybe I should take him
for a walk for a change.

243
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:34,399
Take him outside?!

244
00:15:34,399 --> 00:15:36,999
When everyone sees P-suke, I'm
sure it'll cause a big panic.

245
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,299
Just wait and see.

246
00:15:38,299 --> 00:15:39,799
I'll surprise everyone.

247
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:41,100
A dinosaur pet,

248
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:44,548
I bet will be Japan's...no, the
world's most talked about.

249
00:15:44,548 --> 00:15:47,499
Then they'll take P-suke away.

250
00:15:54,950 --> 00:15:57,900
The scientists will either disect him for research,

251
00:15:57,900 --> 00:16:00,950
Or he'll be put in a zoo for viewing.

252
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:08,150
In either case, it'll be hard for
P-suke to live in this world.

253
00:16:19,050 --> 00:16:20,200
P-suke!

254
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:23,900
P-suke...

255
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:30,100
Soon I'll take you back 100 million
years in the Time Machine, okay?

256
00:16:30,299 --> 00:16:31,499
But, before that...

257
00:16:31,499 --> 00:16:33,699
I have to surprise Suneo.

258
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:39,149
Ahh...it's hot.

259
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:43,650
The bucket water warms up immediately.

260
00:16:43,650 --> 00:16:45,050
Poor thing...

261
00:16:45,050 --> 00:16:48,200
If not outside, how about we
play with water out back?

262
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,050
EH?!

263
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:51,300
Tha-that's still too risky!

264
00:16:54,750 --> 00:16:56,300
Okay, now while we can P-suke.

265
00:17:00,050 --> 00:17:01,950
Do you like it, P-suke?

266
00:17:01,950 --> 00:17:05,700
This is the pool I used in Kindergarten.

267
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:06,700
Nobita

268
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:08,700
Aaaah, Mama!

269
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:11,449
O-0-0-000h, it's been a while
since I've used this pool.

270
00:17:11,449 --> 00:17:14,499
It seems so long ago, that I was reminiscing
my kindergarten years.

271
00:17:16,548 --> 00:17:17,898
Nobita,

272
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:19,900
Tell me the truth.

273
00:17:20,250 --> 00:17:23,950
Lately, the fish and meats have been
disappearing in the refridgerator frequently...

274
00:17:23,950 --> 00:17:26,499
You haven't picked up a stray
cat or dog, have you?

275
00:17:26,499 --> 00:17:29,048
Wha-what? I swear to God, no.

276
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:32,148
If I find out that you have,
you'll be in big trouble...

277
00:17:32,150 --> 00:17:32,900
You hear me?

278
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:33,700
Hai.

279
00:17:36,499 --> 00:17:38,848
If I told her that I have a pet dinosaur,

280
00:17:38,848 --> 00:17:41,298
Mama would probably faint from it.

281
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:42,900
So don't worry, I won't tell her.

282
00:17:59,749 --> 00:18:03,098
He's gotten so big, we can't keep
secretly raise him anymore.

283
00:18:03,098 --> 00:18:05,098
We should take him to the Cretacious
period already...

284
00:18:05,098 --> 00:18:09,898
No, not yet. Not till he gets bigger so
I can make Suneo quack in his shoes.

285
00:18:16,848 --> 00:18:17,698
Doraemon,

286
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:20,200
I let him loose in the pond at the park,
so we don't have to worry anymore.

287
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,098
Park?

288
00:18:21,098 --> 00:18:22,249
He'll be okay.

289
00:18:22,250 --> 00:18:26,349
I made sure he knows not to show
himself unless I call him.

290
00:18:26,350 --> 00:18:29,300
Hmmm....I wonder if it'll work that simple.

291
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:44,000
PI

292
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:56,300
You know it's me by my footsteps?

293
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:57,950
Good boy.

294
00:18:57,950 --> 00:18:59,200
Did you miss me?

295
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:01,500
I'm sorry I can only come here at night.

296
00:19:04,098 --> 00:19:06,648
Tonight's treat is sausage.

297
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:08,650
See?

298
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,350
Here, eat up.

299
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,300
Here.

300
00:19:20,650 --> 00:19:21,848
Sorry. Sorry.

301
00:19:21,848 --> 00:19:22,648
Here.

302
00:19:36,048 --> 00:19:39,249
P-suke, it started to rain, so I'll come back later.

303
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:07,450
P-suke!

304
00:20:47,350 --> 00:20:50,150
P-suke...wonder how he's doing right now...

305
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:54,850
Oh, Doraemon. How was he?

306
00:20:56,098 --> 00:20:58,598
Well, he won't eat at all.

307
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:01,500
Apparently, he misses you.

308
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:06,350
It's been three days since you
got sick and last saw him.

309
00:21:06,350 --> 00:21:07,900
It's no surprise.

310
00:21:13,250 --> 00:21:14,650
What's that sound?

311
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:20,100
Psuke!

312
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:23,000
You're not supposed to be here.

313
00:21:24,150 --> 00:21:25,300
P-suke

314
00:21:26,350 --> 00:21:29,900
What are we going to do if someone
saw you coming here?

315
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:32,700
Nobita-kun, he came to see you.

316
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,450
I see. P-suke.

317
00:21:37,250 --> 00:21:38,499
Please understand.

318
00:21:38,499 --> 00:21:40,949
I would love to visit you everyday too,

319
00:21:40,950 --> 00:21:42,650
So, please be a good boy.

320
00:21:42,950 --> 00:21:43,650
P-suke.

321
00:21:44,749 --> 00:21:45,699
Doraemon,

322
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:48,200
Could you please take P-suke back to the park?

323
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:49,000
Okay.

324
00:21:50,150 --> 00:21:51,300
C'mon. Let's go.

325
00:22:05,350 --> 00:22:08,000
You gotta eat your food, okay?

326
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:14,900
I can't be lollygagging anymore.

327
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:33,499
Hey Suneo,

328
00:22:33,499 --> 00:22:35,848
I'll show you the promised thing tonight.

329
00:22:36,098 --> 00:22:39,798
Oh my, Nobita-chan. It's a holiday
starting today, right?

330
00:22:39,848 --> 00:22:43,698
Suneo-chama has gone to Karuizawa
on an overnighter.

331
00:22:44,350 --> 00:22:46,650
Shizuka-chan went on a one night trip too?

332
00:22:48,098 --> 00:22:50,749
He went with his grandpa on a job
to the mountains to gather straw.

333
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:53,048
Giant too.

334
00:22:53,048 --> 00:22:56,898
Then that means there's no one here.

335
00:22:57,499 --> 00:22:58,598
Did you know?

336
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:01,900
There's a dinosaur in the lake at the park.

337
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:03,400
No way.

338
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:06,300
There are people who said they've seen it.

339
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:07,300
Oh?

340
00:23:07,798 --> 00:23:11,098
The Wildlife Association claims it's impossible, but,

341
00:23:11,098 --> 00:23:13,898
As the rumors spread, this station
cannot stand by idly.

342
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:17,150
And will be employing a submersible to verify...

343
00:23:17,650 --> 00:23:19,499
And, we will update you, as soon as we can.

344
00:23:19,499 --> 00:23:22,298
A A Monster in the Park's Lake.

345
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:25,548
D-d-d-doraemon, w-w-w-hat d-do
we do? What do we do?!

346
00:23:25,548 --> 00:23:28,398
There is only one thing you can do.

347
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:31,300
Return P-suke back to his own
time, 100 million years past.

348
00:23:31,300 --> 00:23:32,150
But..

349
00:23:32,150 --> 00:23:34,098
Spaghetti...

350
00:23:34,098 --> 00:23:37,548
Think about it, it is your dinosaur after all.

351
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:50,100
P-suke...

352
00:23:58,200 --> 00:24:00,100
W-w-who are you?!

353
00:24:01,848 --> 00:24:03,848
You're the one they call Nobita-kun, aren't you?

354
00:24:03,848 --> 00:24:09,898
After observing you and your dinosaur,
we decided we want him for ourselves.

355
00:24:10,200 --> 00:24:13,049
I-won't let you do as you p-please!

356
00:24:13,650 --> 00:24:18,750
I'm leaving for now, but know that
I will return for your dinosaur.

357
00:24:29,848 --> 00:24:31,298
There's no turning back

358
00:24:31,300 --> 00:24:34,300
I have to return P-suke to his
time 100 milion years past.

359
00:24:57,300 --> 00:24:59,350
Doraemon, Small Light

360
00:24:59,350 --> 00:25:00,000
Yeah.

361
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:01,500
Here.

362
00:25:18,900 --> 00:25:20,200
Doraemon, let's hurry.

363
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:20,850
Yeah.

364
00:25:29,700 --> 00:25:31,000
That was not cool.

365
00:25:37,250 --> 00:25:38,349
P-suke

366
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,950
Just a bit more.

367
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:41,799
What was that?

368
00:25:42,700 --> 00:25:43,900
Wait!

369
00:25:44,250 --> 00:25:48,299
As promised, I have come for that dinosaur.

370
00:25:48,848 --> 00:25:50,598
It's the man in black from before.

371
00:25:50,600 --> 00:25:51,499
You know him?

372
00:25:51,499 --> 00:25:52,499
He's bad.

373
00:25:52,499 --> 00:25:55,098
He's come to kidnap P-suke.

374
00:25:55,098 --> 00:25:56,298
Okay.

375
00:25:59,499 --> 00:26:00,798
Wait!

376
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:06,050
Tenacious kids.

377
00:26:08,548 --> 00:26:11,298
Now hand over that dinosaur!

378
00:26:16,600 --> 00:26:17,900
Uh-oh.

379
00:27:03,300 --> 00:27:04,798
Doraemon, Big Light.

380
00:27:04,798 --> 00:27:05,499
Yeah.

381
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:14,700
P-suke, this is your world.

382
00:27:19,150 --> 00:27:21,600
Live a happy life here, you hear?

383
00:27:24,798 --> 00:27:26,148
Take care then.

384
00:27:26,600 --> 00:27:27,499
Goodbye.

385
00:27:27,499 --> 00:27:28,098
Let's go.

386
00:27:33,098 --> 00:27:35,048
A-a-ah. Hey. Hey.

387
00:27:35,650 --> 00:27:36,200
No.

388
00:27:36,950 --> 00:27:38,750
You're not supposed to follow us!

389
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,000
You hear?!

390
00:28:03,048 --> 00:28:03,949
No!

391
00:28:06,449 --> 00:28:09,298
P-suke! This is the best place for you to live!

392
00:28:12,499 --> 00:28:15,098
Don't you understand?

393
00:28:20,449 --> 00:28:21,749
Doraemon, let's go!

394
00:28:21,749 --> 00:28:21,999
Yeah!

395
00:29:58,449 --> 00:30:01,499
This time you didn't rely on me.

396
00:30:01,499 --> 00:30:04,298
And thought things through,

397
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:06,450
Which is a significant improvement.

398
00:30:23,200 --> 00:30:25,950
Hey! Nobita!

399
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:34,250
Nobita! You promised to eat
spaghetti through your nose.

400
00:30:34,250 --> 00:30:36,849
Nobita-kun, it's Giant and Suneo.

401
00:30:39,098 --> 00:30:40,499
What are you going to do?

402
00:30:46,300 --> 00:30:49,400
You promised, now I wanna see you
eat that spaghetti with your nose.

403
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:53,798
B-but, I did raise a whole dinosaur, so.

404
00:30:53,798 --> 00:30:55,098
I really did.

405
00:30:55,098 --> 00:30:56,848
He's still saying it.

406
00:30:57,350 --> 00:30:59,400
Have you no shame?

407
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:01,650
You gotta believe me, I'm telling you the truth.

408
00:31:01,650 --> 00:31:02,798
Shut up!

409
00:31:02,798 --> 00:31:04,398
Here! Eat it!

410
00:31:04,400 --> 00:31:05,749
Mgh-ghugh

411
00:31:05,749 --> 00:31:07,298
With your nose, eat it with your nose.
Mgh-ghugh

412
00:31:08,900 --> 00:31:10,200
ACHOO!!

413
00:31:14,900 --> 00:31:16,100
Wait!!

414
00:31:21,848 --> 00:31:22,698
Shizuka-chan.

415
00:31:22,700 --> 00:31:25,150
What are you doing up there?

416
00:31:25,150 --> 00:31:26,950
...um...

417
00:31:29,749 --> 00:31:32,399
I'm sorry. I'm being chased by Suneo and Giant.

418
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:34,150
The thing you promised?

419
00:31:35,749 --> 00:31:37,399
Just let me hide here.

420
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:43,349
Well, it was a ridiculous deal you made there.

421
00:31:43,350 --> 00:31:46,449
There are no living dinosaurs.

422
00:31:46,449 --> 00:31:49,499
And you can't eat spaghetti with your nose.

423
00:31:49,798 --> 00:31:53,298
If you go and apologize now, you guys will
be laughing about the whole thing later.

424
00:31:53,300 --> 00:31:54,098
But...

425
00:31:54,098 --> 00:31:56,749
But I did raise a dinosaur.

426
00:31:56,749 --> 00:31:57,548
My.

427
00:31:58,200 --> 00:32:01,299
Everyone lies when pressured sometime.

428
00:32:01,300 --> 00:32:03,499
But being stubborn about it,

429
00:32:03,499 --> 00:32:05,499
Is really unmanly.

430
00:32:07,650 --> 00:32:09,098
If you insist, I'll show you.

431
00:32:09,098 --> 00:32:10,749
I'll show you alright!

432
00:32:14,700 --> 00:32:16,299
Hey, Doraemon.

433
00:32:16,700 --> 00:32:20,450
Can we at least show P-suke on the Time TV.

434
00:32:22,650 --> 00:32:24,300
It wouldn't be so bad if we just
watched him on TV, right?

435
00:32:30,700 --> 00:32:31,650
Sure.

436
00:32:32,200 --> 00:32:33,650
All right.

437
00:32:40,900 --> 00:32:41,850
P-suke!

438
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:11,500
What's going on?

439
00:33:12,650 --> 00:33:14,350
This is bad!

440
00:33:14,350 --> 00:33:15,250
What?

441
00:33:15,749 --> 00:33:18,598
P-suke is a Japanese Plesiosaur

442
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:21,900
And we sent him to the wrong place.

443
00:33:21,900 --> 00:33:22,600
WHAT?

444
00:33:22,749 --> 00:33:25,298
The Time Machine can go
to the past and future.

445
00:33:25,300 --> 00:33:27,749
In other words, it travels through time.

446
00:33:27,749 --> 00:33:32,048
But it also can move here and there,

447
00:33:32,048 --> 00:33:34,249
Which means it also has a spatial function.

448
00:33:34,250 --> 00:33:38,299
The man in black damaged the
spatial control mechanism,

449
00:33:38,300 --> 00:33:39,900
Which caused this.

450
00:33:41,950 --> 00:33:43,900
What wrong place do you think we sent him?

451
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:45,700
Looks like...

452
00:33:45,700 --> 00:33:47,200
The North American Continent.

453
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:48,749
That is serious!

454
00:33:48,749 --> 00:33:52,899
Doraemon, let's go get P-suke and take
him to Japan in the Cretacious period.

455
00:33:53,449 --> 00:33:55,899
Hurry, Doraemon, hurry!

456
00:33:57,200 --> 00:33:59,299
Ow-ow-ow-ow.

457
00:33:59,300 --> 00:34:02,900
We'll go too. We can, can't we? Right?

458
00:34:02,900 --> 00:34:06,050
You can't all fit. It'll be over the weight limit.

459
00:34:38,899 --> 00:34:41,199
Doraemon

460
00:34:41,250 --> 00:34:43,199
Aaaagh

461
00:35:33,250 --> 00:35:37,250
What's the deal? Doraemon,
you botched the landing.

462
00:35:37,250 --> 00:35:38,500
Where is Doraemon?

463
00:35:39,748 --> 00:35:42,448
What will happen to us if
We can't find Doraemon?

464
00:35:45,349 --> 00:35:49,049
Doraemon.

465
00:35:53,699 --> 00:35:54,699
Over there

466
00:36:05,349 --> 00:36:06,449
Doraemon.

467
00:36:06,449 --> 00:36:10,149
Goodness, gracious, Doraemon.

468
00:36:11,899 --> 00:36:12,648
Over there

469
00:36:12,648 --> 00:36:14,498
We left P-suke over there.

470
00:36:14,500 --> 00:36:15,599
Yahoo!

471
00:36:38,598 --> 00:36:42,398
P-suke!

472
00:36:57,699 --> 00:36:59,148
P-suke.

473
00:37:05,699 --> 00:37:06,499
It's P-suke!

474
00:37:06,500 --> 00:37:07,500
Yahoo!

475
00:37:09,699 --> 00:37:11,648
P-suke!

476
00:37:14,199 --> 00:37:15,299
P-suke!

477
00:37:16,449 --> 00:37:17,399
P-suke!

478
00:37:17,598 --> 00:37:20,198
P-suke..P!

479
00:37:29,648 --> 00:37:30,699
P-suke.

480
00:37:30,699 --> 00:37:32,699
I missed you, P-suke.

481
00:37:39,500 --> 00:37:40,699
I'm not worthy.

482
00:37:40,699 --> 00:37:41,398
You win.

483
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:42,500
I'm sorry.

484
00:37:42,500 --> 00:37:44,650
I apologize for not believing you.

485
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:46,798
It's okay.

486
00:37:46,798 --> 00:37:48,949
But, see, I was telling the truth.

487
00:37:52,899 --> 00:37:55,899
It's real. It's a real Futaba-Suzuki-Ryu.

488
00:37:56,449 --> 00:37:57,199
Gah?

489
00:38:04,899 --> 00:38:06,798
He's cute.

490
00:38:06,798 --> 00:38:07,148
Over here.

491
00:38:08,048 --> 00:38:09,699
He's tame.
Over here, over here.

492
00:38:14,699 --> 00:38:15,898
I can't fix it.

493
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:23,099
Elasmosaurus platyurus.

494
00:38:23,449 --> 00:38:28,299
Even though it's a Plesiosaur, the American
one differs from the Japanese.

495
00:38:29,250 --> 00:38:31,500
So that's why they're unfriendly.

496
00:38:31,500 --> 00:38:36,400
Don't worry, P-suke, we're here
to take you back to Japan.

497
00:39:09,500 --> 00:39:10,300
Doraemon,

498
00:39:10,500 --> 00:39:13,250
Let's hurry and take P-suke back to Japan.

499
00:39:13,648 --> 00:39:15,898
Uh, about that...

500
00:39:15,899 --> 00:39:18,798
Since we're here, 100 million years in the past,

501
00:39:18,798 --> 00:39:23,648
How about we camp here overnight,
and go home tomorrow?

502
00:39:24,500 --> 00:39:28,598
Woo hoo, woo hoo, it's camp
time, it's camp time.

503
00:39:28,598 --> 00:39:29,448
But I haven't finished my homework,

504
00:39:29,449 --> 00:39:33,549
And I'll get in trouble if I stay over anywhere
without asking my mom.

505
00:39:33,550 --> 00:39:35,648
Yeah, yeah, Doraemon!

506
00:39:35,648 --> 00:39:37,199
Don't say things irresponsibly!

507
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:38,900
Well...

508
00:39:41,500 --> 00:39:42,798
It's not a problem.

509
00:39:42,798 --> 00:39:44,699
We came in the Time Machine,

510
00:39:44,699 --> 00:39:47,898
So it doesn't matter if we stay
here for a days or even years.

511
00:39:47,899 --> 00:39:53,899
If we set it to five minutes after we left,
we'll only be gone for five minutes.

512
00:39:54,500 --> 00:39:55,299
Let's play.

513
00:39:55,299 --> 00:39:56,899
Let's swim with P-suke.

514
00:39:56,899 --> 00:39:58,399
Agreed!

515
00:39:59,849 --> 00:40:01,048
One moment.

516
00:40:02,048 --> 00:40:05,099
You can make swimsuits with
this Kisekae Camera

517
00:40:05,299 --> 00:40:08,399
You can draw your favorite
designs in this notebook.

518
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:10,849
Leave the designing to me.

519
00:40:14,798 --> 00:40:15,798
This should do it.

520
00:40:17,798 --> 00:40:18,349
Here.

521
00:40:20,748 --> 00:40:23,448
Everyone line up, line up.

522
00:40:37,048 --> 00:40:38,449
Eeek

523
00:40:39,149 --> 00:40:40,249
Oops, sorry.

524
00:40:49,748 --> 00:40:51,248
And then,

525
00:40:51,349 --> 00:40:55,150
With this Air-tube you can breath underwater,

526
00:40:55,500 --> 00:40:59,500
And with this Shinkai Cream you can withstand
any water temperature and water pressure.

527
00:40:59,648 --> 00:41:00,148
Wow.

528
00:41:01,349 --> 00:41:04,849
Yippee!

529
00:41:59,299 --> 00:42:00,749
You're so cute.

530
00:42:02,550 --> 00:42:03,900
Beautiful.

531
00:42:06,598 --> 00:42:08,348
What's this, what's this?

532
00:42:08,349 --> 00:42:10,049
Ah, an Ammonite

533
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:59,199
That's interesting

534
00:42:59,199 --> 00:43:01,849
Doraemon, your pocket even has food.

535
00:43:01,849 --> 00:43:03,849
I want to eat something better.

536
00:43:04,299 --> 00:43:06,699
It's a luxury in this age.

537
00:43:06,699 --> 00:43:09,648
If the dinosaurs find us, we're the meal.

538
00:43:09,699 --> 00:43:10,499
Right?

539
00:43:10,949 --> 00:43:12,500
What's the matter, Dora-chan?

540
00:43:13,149 --> 00:43:14,899
O-oh, it's nothing.

541
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:16,500
You're a funny one, Doraemon.

542
00:43:16,849 --> 00:43:17,699
Anyway,

543
00:43:17,699 --> 00:43:20,449
When you say 100 million years ago,

544
00:43:20,449 --> 00:43:23,449
How long ago, would 100 million years be?

545
00:43:23,648 --> 00:43:26,298
Well, it's one year 100 million times.

546
00:43:26,299 --> 00:43:29,299
But that doesn't really put it into perspective.

547
00:43:29,299 --> 00:43:32,299
Isn't there a better way to describe it?

548
00:43:33,648 --> 00:43:35,148
That's impossible.

549
00:43:35,648 --> 00:43:36,598
For example,

550
00:43:36,798 --> 00:43:40,148
When we hear stories about our grandparents,

551
00:43:40,149 --> 00:43:42,499
Even though it seems long ago,

552
00:43:42,500 --> 00:43:45,199
In reality, it would be at most 60 years, right?

553
00:43:45,199 --> 00:43:45,798
Umm...

554
00:43:45,798 --> 00:43:48,648
If you divide 100 million by 60

555
00:43:48,648 --> 00:43:51,699
That means grandpa's, grandpa's grandpa...

556
00:43:51,699 --> 00:43:54,298
I can't figure it out.

557
00:43:54,299 --> 00:43:55,048
I thought so.

558
00:43:55,048 --> 00:43:58,349
Anyhow, let's just say we came
pretty far back in time.

559
00:44:08,748 --> 00:44:11,298
History is mystifying.

560
00:44:21,400 --> 00:44:23,299
Since we finished dinner,

561
00:44:23,299 --> 00:44:26,449
I would like to take this moment
to give you my recital.

562
00:44:26,598 --> 00:44:28,448
Giant, you're gonna sing?

563
00:44:28,748 --> 00:44:30,498
You got a problem with that, Nobita?

564
00:44:30,500 --> 00:44:32,750
N-no, please sing

565
00:44:32,949 --> 00:44:34,049
Really?

566
00:44:34,699 --> 00:44:38,499
Dora-dora give it to them don-don-don.

567
00:44:38,500 --> 00:44:42,598
I am a lively King.

568
00:44:42,598 --> 00:44:46,298
Just like fireworks, don-don-don

569
00:44:46,299 --> 00:44:48,149
I'm a prankster.

570
00:44:48,149 --> 00:44:49,999
From up close I go don.

571
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:53,648
When school is over, I'm already there.

572
00:44:53,648 --> 00:44:57,449
And to tomorrow, it's just as fun as today.

573
00:44:57,449 --> 00:45:01,099
I'm Giant, full of energy.

574
00:45:01,099 --> 00:45:04,949
And when tomorrow comes,
I'll have just as much fun.

575
00:45:04,949 --> 00:45:08,500
I am Giant, the energetic...

576
00:45:09,099 --> 00:45:10,699
St-stop, stop Giant!

577
00:45:10,699 --> 00:45:13,099
The dinosaurs are gonna react to your singing!

578
00:45:13,099 --> 00:45:14,099
What did you say?!

579
00:45:14,099 --> 00:45:15,899
That won't happen!

580
00:45:15,899 --> 00:45:19,699
Da d-da-da give it to them don-don-don!

581
00:45:19,699 --> 00:45:22,798
I am Giant, full of energy!

582
00:45:22,798 --> 00:45:24,349
G-Giant!

583
00:45:35,550 --> 00:45:38,300
D-Doraemon, help us.

584
00:45:42,099 --> 00:45:45,099
Doraemon, what are you doing?

585
00:46:10,449 --> 00:46:11,849
I've had enough!

586
00:46:11,849 --> 00:46:13,399
Let's go home already!

587
00:46:13,849 --> 00:46:14,598
Yeah.

588
00:46:14,598 --> 00:46:17,898
Let's take P-suke to the twentieth
century with us.

589
00:46:24,899 --> 00:46:26,199
EHH?!

590
00:46:26,500 --> 00:46:28,550
We can't go home?!

591
00:46:28,550 --> 00:46:30,849
What do you mean?!

592
00:46:30,849 --> 00:46:32,099
To be frank,

593
00:46:32,099 --> 00:46:35,648
The traveling space device on the
Time Machine has been broken.

594
00:46:35,648 --> 00:46:37,248
It can't be fixed.

595
00:46:37,250 --> 00:46:40,449
In other words, we can't go home?

596
00:46:40,449 --> 00:46:43,199
Well...we can still travel time.

597
00:46:43,199 --> 00:46:47,399
So for an example, if we carry this Time
Machine to where Japan would be,

598
00:46:47,400 --> 00:46:51,550
No, the Japan Islands weren't formed
yet back a 100 million years ago.

599
00:46:51,550 --> 00:46:53,899
Where it would be in the future,

600
00:46:53,899 --> 00:46:55,798
And to be exact, Tokyo's...

601
00:46:55,798 --> 00:46:57,449
Nobita-kun's residence,

602
00:46:57,449 --> 00:46:59,000
In Nobita-kun's room...

603
00:46:59,000 --> 00:47:00,598
Nobita-kun's desk...

604
00:47:00,598 --> 00:47:03,398
If we could put this Time Machine
on the exact position...

605
00:47:03,400 --> 00:47:05,400
It's possible we can get back home.

606
00:47:06,048 --> 00:47:08,398
But there's no way that that's possible.

607
00:47:16,400 --> 00:47:18,149
Oknow. Doraemon,

608
00:47:18,149 --> 00:47:19,899
Let's fly by the Take-copters.

609
00:47:20,899 --> 00:47:21,748
No!

610
00:47:21,748 --> 00:47:24,498
Take-copters fastest speed is 80 km,

611
00:47:24,500 --> 00:47:27,949
If we use it continuously for eight
hours, the battery will die.

612
00:47:27,949 --> 00:47:30,449
We can only go 640 km.

613
00:47:30,449 --> 00:47:33,099
How much more distance do
you think it is to Japan?

614
00:47:33,099 --> 00:47:35,099
Oh no...

615
00:47:36,048 --> 00:47:38,648
Hey, hey, you piece of trash robot!

616
00:47:39,550 --> 00:47:44,149
How dare you bring us to such
a place with a broken machine!

617
00:47:44,149 --> 00:47:45,798
What the Hell are you talking about, Giant!

618
00:47:45,798 --> 00:47:47,849
You were the one who jumped
in without asking.

619
00:47:47,849 --> 00:47:51,099
That's why...that's why this happened
because of the overload.

620
00:47:51,099 --> 00:47:52,849
What was that?!

621
00:47:53,949 --> 00:47:54,500
Hey,

622
00:47:54,500 --> 00:47:56,099
Everyone, listen up.

623
00:47:58,000 --> 00:48:00,099
When we were playing with
the radio controller,

624
00:48:00,099 --> 00:48:03,899
The battery died when it was
continuously played with,

625
00:48:03,899 --> 00:48:05,798
But when we let it rest here and there,

626
00:48:05,798 --> 00:48:07,599
It lasts a long time, remember?

627
00:48:07,699 --> 00:48:11,798
Maybe we can apply that to the Take-copters?

628
00:48:12,299 --> 00:48:13,099
Yeah.

629
00:48:13,099 --> 00:48:14,748
Doraemon, it can, can't it?

630
00:48:14,748 --> 00:48:16,448
It'll last longer, right?

631
00:48:16,798 --> 00:48:20,148
YAY! We can go back home to Japan!!

632
00:48:20,149 --> 00:48:20,699
Wait.

633
00:48:21,400 --> 00:48:23,000
Where are we going to let it rest?

634
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:27,299
Between America and Japan, there's
the huge Pacific Ocean you know.

635
00:48:27,299 --> 00:48:31,449
Hey, Suneo! How dare you talk nonsense to us.

636
00:48:31,449 --> 00:48:31,699
No!

637
00:48:31,699 --> 00:48:33,048
He's talking good sense.

638
00:48:35,149 --> 00:48:39,598
Hey, hey, within the 100 million years,
the Earth has changed drastically.

639
00:48:39,598 --> 00:48:44,648
So in this era, the Asian Continent
and America were connected.

640
00:48:44,899 --> 00:48:46,749
see...

641
00:48:47,400 --> 00:48:48,748
Then...

642
00:48:48,748 --> 00:48:50,748
We can get home then?

643
00:48:50,748 --> 00:48:51,698
To Japan?

644
00:48:51,699 --> 00:48:52,349
Yup!

645
00:48:53,598 --> 00:48:56,548
YAY~!

646
00:48:56,550 --> 00:48:57,849
We can go home!

647
00:48:57,849 --> 00:49:02,099
We can go home to Japan!

648
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:16,300
Hey, P-suke!

649
00:49:35,648 --> 00:49:36,898
Come on, jump in.

650
00:49:38,250 --> 00:49:39,550
Ok, let's take off!

651
00:50:36,899 --> 00:50:38,449
It's just a little ways more.

652
00:50:38,449 --> 00:50:40,500
I'll take you out as soon as I can, okay P-suke?

653
00:50:46,899 --> 00:50:50,749
Let's stop here today, and make
a camp at that beach there.

654
00:50:59,149 --> 00:50:59,849
Doraemon,

655
00:51:00,048 --> 00:51:01,099
Take out the Big Light.

656
00:51:01,099 --> 00:51:01,699
Here.

657
00:51:07,449 --> 00:51:07,949
There.

658
00:51:14,149 --> 00:51:16,598
We're going to camp here till morning.

659
00:51:16,598 --> 00:51:18,098
Don't go far, okay?

660
00:51:20,449 --> 00:51:21,649
Hey, hey, hey.

661
00:51:23,798 --> 00:51:27,248
What? No, I'm busy.

662
00:51:27,250 --> 00:51:28,500
Go on, go play!

663
00:51:36,349 --> 00:51:37,299
Um...

664
00:51:37,699 --> 00:51:39,749
Camping Capsule!

665
00:51:40,449 --> 00:51:41,599
Um...

666
00:51:42,748 --> 00:51:44,498
Where shall l...

667
00:51:44,500 --> 00:51:46,349
Ummmm...

668
00:52:05,099 --> 00:52:06,899
Okay everyone, jump on.

669
00:52:25,250 --> 00:52:28,800
Our long journal has finally started.

670
00:52:31,099 --> 00:52:32,648
Yahooo~!

671
00:52:32,648 --> 00:52:34,098
This is great.

672
00:52:35,849 --> 00:52:37,199
Dear Mother...

673
00:53:44,299 --> 00:53:45,649
Hey, over here!

674
00:53:53,899 --> 00:53:55,149
I can't walk anymore.

675
00:53:55,149 --> 00:53:56,799
Take out the Take-copter.

676
00:53:57,299 --> 00:53:58,149
Please?

677
00:54:00,099 --> 00:54:00,899
No!

678
00:54:00,899 --> 00:54:02,699
Is it okay if you don't return to Japan?

679
00:54:02,699 --> 00:54:03,499
You need to walk!

680
00:54:10,699 --> 00:54:12,249
Perfect!

681
00:54:13,699 --> 00:54:16,449
Momotaro Brand, Kibidango.

682
00:54:29,250 --> 00:54:31,750
Come on, let us ride you.

683
00:55:37,299 --> 00:55:40,199
Wow. It's a real Brontosaurus.

684
00:55:40,199 --> 00:55:42,000
It's not a fossil or a stuffed animal,

685
00:55:42,000 --> 00:55:44,149
It's a real breathing Brontosaurus.

686
00:55:44,149 --> 00:55:46,099
AHHHH, this is great!

687
00:55:46,099 --> 00:55:48,598
What are you talking about? What if it eats you?

688
00:55:48,598 --> 00:55:49,848
It's fine.

689
00:55:49,849 --> 00:55:53,798
The Brontosaurus are herbivores
and calm. They're also slow.

690
00:55:53,798 --> 00:55:57,949
As long as you be careful not to be stepped
on, you can get close to them.

691
00:56:06,949 --> 00:56:09,399
Let's go Suneo. Hurry up and follow.

692
00:56:24,648 --> 00:56:26,898
Watch out! Watch out!

693
00:56:35,699 --> 00:56:38,849
Yay, it's a slide.

694
00:56:52,648 --> 00:56:54,199
Wah, so cute.

695
00:56:58,699 --> 00:57:00,699
Hey everyone, take a look at this.

696
00:57:01,500 --> 00:57:02,500
What is it?

697
00:57:04,349 --> 00:57:05,549
See?

698
00:57:07,949 --> 00:57:10,299
It's such a cute newly born.

699
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:30,250
www

700
00:58:24,400 --> 00:58:26,500
Oh no, the baby!

701
00:58:32,798 --> 00:58:33,898
Ah, Shizuka-chan.

702
00:58:34,449 --> 00:58:35,599
Ah, hey...

703
00:58:42,299 --> 00:58:43,849
You need to run with us!

704
00:59:05,500 --> 00:59:07,300
We got caught!

705
00:59:12,299 --> 00:59:14,099
Do--Doraemon...

706
00:59:15,598 --> 00:59:17,598
Oh, no. Not this...

707
00:59:17,598 --> 00:59:19,498
It's not this, or that!

708
00:59:19,500 --> 00:59:20,900
OH, not this either!

709
00:59:26,048 --> 00:59:28,148
Momotaro Brand Kibidango!

710
00:59:28,849 --> 00:59:29,849
There!

711
00:59:35,699 --> 00:59:36,898
That was close.

712
00:59:36,899 --> 00:59:38,899
Tyrannosaurus is our follower now.

713
00:59:38,899 --> 00:59:40,899
You can play with it now.

714
00:59:41,299 --> 00:59:42,648
Really?
Are you sure?

715
00:59:42,648 --> 00:59:43,449
Really?

716
00:59:43,449 --> 00:59:44,199
See?

717
00:59:44,199 --> 00:59:44,849
Hey!

718
00:59:44,849 --> 00:59:45,849
Yay!

719
00:59:47,299 --> 00:59:48,899
I'm gonna make this my first findings.

720
00:59:48,899 --> 00:59:50,699
Hey, Doraemon!

721
00:59:50,699 --> 00:59:51,548
Shizuka-chan!

722
00:59:51,550 --> 00:59:52,750
Shall we?

723
00:59:55,250 --> 00:59:56,550
Take off!

724
01:00:24,748 --> 01:00:25,848
Dear Mother...

725
01:00:32,000 --> 01:00:33,798
Even though we were faced
with different incidents,

726
01:00:33,798 --> 01:00:37,449
The crossing of the American
Continent is going well.

727
01:00:42,299 --> 01:00:44,799
Mommy, forgive me!

728
01:01:10,048 --> 01:01:11,048
Do-Doraemon!

729
01:01:12,699 --> 01:01:14,398
The Take-copter is broken!

730
01:01:14,400 --> 01:01:17,250
As soon as we find a good spot, let's land early.

731
01:01:26,648 --> 01:01:28,498
Nobita, stop being a slowpoke.

732
01:01:28,500 --> 01:01:31,500
When you're slow, it makes
a burden for the rest of us.

733
01:01:31,500 --> 01:01:34,449
Nobita's slowness has infected his Take-copter.

734
01:01:36,349 --> 01:01:39,599
You shouldn't say such a thing
when he's in trouble!

735
01:01:39,949 --> 01:01:40,849
Are you okay?

736
01:01:40,849 --> 01:01:41,449
Yeah.

737
01:01:41,449 --> 01:01:42,250
Shizuka-chan...

738
01:01:43,699 --> 01:01:45,099
You can do it. We're almost there.

739
01:01:45,099 --> 01:01:45,649
Yeah.

740
01:01:52,849 --> 01:01:54,349
It's a Pterodactyl!

741
01:01:55,099 --> 01:01:56,849
Hey, wait for me!

742
01:02:33,199 --> 01:02:35,099
Kibidango! Kibidango! Kibidango!

743
01:02:36,400 --> 01:02:37,500
Found it!

744
01:02:41,899 --> 01:02:43,249
Oh darn...

745
01:03:37,199 --> 01:03:39,199
Who are you guys?

746
01:03:39,199 --> 01:03:41,449
Why are you guys following us?

747
01:03:41,449 --> 01:03:44,299
You know, don't you? We
want your P-suke-kun.

748
01:03:44,299 --> 01:03:45,199
Huh?

749
01:03:48,099 --> 01:03:49,099
You can't!

750
01:03:49,099 --> 01:03:53,899
I've been killing numerous dinosaurs
mainly of this era,

751
01:03:53,899 --> 01:03:55,499
Or even catching them.

752
01:03:55,500 --> 01:03:58,648
I've never seen such a human
friendly dinosaur as P-suke.

753
01:03:58,648 --> 01:04:00,898
really want to have him.

754
01:04:01,449 --> 01:04:02,299
I see!

755
01:04:02,299 --> 01:04:05,899
What's a dinosaur hunter?

756
01:04:05,899 --> 01:04:08,949
There's this time traveling law
called the Posted Law,

757
01:04:08,949 --> 01:04:12,798
You're forbidden to capture creatures
from the pass without permission.

758
01:04:12,798 --> 01:04:14,998
Because it'll change the history.

759
01:04:15,000 --> 01:04:21,500
For example, the ancestors of humans are living
somewhere in this era as mammals and reptiles.

760
01:04:21,500 --> 01:04:23,250
What will happen if they are killed?

761
01:04:23,250 --> 01:04:26,748
It'll mean that humans were
never born on this Earth.

762
01:04:26,748 --> 01:04:29,648
It'll mean that none of you would exist.

763
01:04:29,648 --> 01:04:31,298
It's nothing that serious.

764
01:04:31,299 --> 01:04:32,899
There are tons of dinosaurs.

765
01:04:32,899 --> 01:04:35,449
It doesn't make a difference if we catch a few.

766
01:04:35,699 --> 01:04:37,849
But you're breaking the law!

767
01:04:37,849 --> 01:04:39,699
And for a profit!

768
01:04:39,849 --> 01:04:41,499
There are rich people,

769
01:04:41,500 --> 01:04:45,750
Who want stuffed Pterodactyl or the neck
of a Tyrannosaurus to put on their wall!

770
01:04:46,048 --> 01:04:46,898
How could they?!

771
01:04:46,899 --> 01:04:49,699
Like we could hand over P-suke
to such bad people!

772
01:04:51,149 --> 01:04:54,299
Come on, you shouldn't jump to conclusions.

773
01:04:54,299 --> 01:04:55,748
I'm not saying we want him for free.

774
01:04:55,748 --> 01:04:57,898
On top of giving you tons of money,

775
01:04:57,899 --> 01:05:01,049
We're willing to take you back to your era.

776
01:05:01,299 --> 01:05:03,499
You're gonna take us back home?

777
01:05:03,648 --> 01:05:04,348
Yes.

778
01:05:04,648 --> 01:05:07,048
Talk it over amongst yourselves tonight,

779
01:05:07,048 --> 01:05:08,648
Then come to our base.

780
01:05:08,648 --> 01:05:14,098
We made it underground, just on the other side of
that waterfall, so the Time Patrol can't find us.

781
01:05:14,699 --> 01:05:15,949
Like Hell we're going!!

782
01:05:16,648 --> 01:05:18,248
So...you don't want to?

783
01:05:18,400 --> 01:05:21,299
Then, we'll see you in the morning.
Hope to hear a good decision.

784
01:05:21,299 --> 01:05:23,599
I'm a gentle-hearted man,

785
01:05:24,648 --> 01:05:25,298
See ya

786
01:06:03,099 --> 01:06:04,199
I can't take this no more!

787
01:06:04,199 --> 01:06:05,699
I want to go back to Japan!

788
01:06:05,699 --> 01:06:07,298
I had enough of adventuring!

789
01:06:07,899 --> 01:06:08,798
But...

790
01:06:08,798 --> 01:06:10,898
That's not good for P-suke-chan.

791
01:06:14,899 --> 01:06:17,048
But, it's not like he's going to be eaten up, right?

792
01:06:17,048 --> 01:06:19,298
He'll be sold to a rich person from the future,

793
01:06:19,299 --> 01:06:21,349
And kept in their pool or something, right?

794
01:06:21,349 --> 01:06:24,099
Do you think that's happiness for P-suke?

795
01:06:24,099 --> 01:06:28,298
We have worked so hard
so that wouldn't happen.

796
01:06:28,299 --> 01:06:30,748
Then, if we turn down his offer,

797
01:06:30,748 --> 01:06:34,098
How do you intend on us getting back to Japan?

798
01:06:34,099 --> 01:06:35,899
That's...

799
01:07:06,500 --> 01:07:07,900
P-suke...

800
01:07:22,949 --> 01:07:25,500
We can't just not care for P-suke-chan.

801
01:07:27,899 --> 01:07:29,798
Suneo-kun, you feel the same, right?

802
01:07:29,798 --> 01:07:32,298
Ye-yeah, if you all agree...

803
01:08:45,399 --> 01:08:46,548
Yah, so it's you?

804
01:08:46,550 --> 01:08:49,550
Did you get it? That human-friendly dinosaur?

805
01:08:49,550 --> 01:08:51,949
It's as good as ours.

806
01:08:51,949 --> 01:08:56,449
I was thinking that maybe you should
be the one to capture it on your own.

807
01:08:56,698 --> 01:09:00,548
Since there's no way that the boy who
owns him will give him up easily.

808
01:09:00,550 --> 01:09:03,149
We're probably going to be faced with
a bit of a commotion tomorrow.

809
01:09:03,149 --> 01:09:07,500
Mister, you haven't yet experienced
human hunting, have you?

810
01:09:08,800 --> 01:09:09,850
Okay, let's do it.

811
01:09:09,850 --> 01:09:13,298
Number seven base? It's midway
of Northern America, is it?

812
01:09:13,298 --> 01:09:15,548
Well then, we shall we waiting for you.

813
01:10:10,899 --> 01:10:14,199
A buggie car...where did they hide it?

814
01:10:18,698 --> 01:10:20,498
This is the last warning,

815
01:10:20,500 --> 01:10:22,500
Hand over the dinosaur quietly!

816
01:11:01,698 --> 01:11:02,698
This is...

817
01:11:05,100 --> 01:11:06,850
This is a mud puppet too.

818
01:11:08,698 --> 01:11:09,948
Damn.

819
01:11:09,949 --> 01:11:12,500
Diverting us to such a thing...

820
01:11:12,500 --> 01:11:14,449
Where did the real ones go?

821
01:11:14,449 --> 01:11:15,750
Follow the radio waves.

822
01:11:15,750 --> 01:11:18,298
If they're using a radio controller,
then they have to be somewhere!

823
01:11:18,298 --> 01:11:18,849
Yes!

824
01:11:18,850 --> 01:11:19,850
We've been tricked...

825
01:11:24,899 --> 01:11:29,099
They said their base was hidden
behind the waterfall, right?

826
01:11:29,100 --> 01:11:30,150
Yeah.

827
01:11:39,100 --> 01:11:45,449
They probably would never think that we'd sneak into their
base and use their Time Machine to get back, would they?

828
01:11:45,449 --> 01:11:50,300
But, I don't think we can hold them off
with those clay puppets for long.

829
01:11:50,899 --> 01:11:52,899
The radio controller isn't working anymore.

830
01:11:52,899 --> 01:11:53,599
EH?

831
01:12:12,698 --> 01:12:13,448
Darn!

832
01:12:13,449 --> 01:12:14,500
They've found us!

833
01:14:16,050 --> 01:14:20,449
UC'FC GOING TO TAKE OVER THE TING
NACHING AND FCTURN TO JAPAN.

834
01:14:21,100 --> 01:14:23,100
Take over the Time Machine?!

835
01:14:23,100 --> 01:14:24,500
Unforgiveable!

836
01:14:25,100 --> 01:14:27,349
I was nice thinking that they were kids,

837
01:14:27,349 --> 01:14:29,598
But this is as far as I hold back.

838
01:14:29,598 --> 01:14:32,398
No, no. We have their bait.

839
01:14:32,399 --> 01:14:35,099
We know for sure that the remaining
two are headed here.

840
01:14:35,100 --> 01:14:37,200
Shall we prepare to greet them?

841
01:14:39,698 --> 01:14:40,298
Hurry!

842
01:14:41,199 --> 01:14:41,849
Understood!

843
01:15:21,750 --> 01:15:22,649
P-suke.

844
01:15:23,298 --> 01:15:26,399
Doraemon!

845
01:15:27,850 --> 01:15:28,648
Nobita-kun.

846
01:15:28,648 --> 01:15:29,398
Ah, Doraemon!
Nobita-kun.

847
01:15:30,100 --> 01:15:30,950
P-suke.

848
01:15:31,349 --> 01:15:33,298
I'm glad we found you.

849
01:15:33,750 --> 01:15:34,899
No-Nobita-kun...

850
01:15:34,899 --> 01:15:36,500
That, that!

851
01:16:19,698 --> 01:16:20,498
P-suke,

852
01:16:20,500 --> 01:16:22,000
You need to hold on.

853
01:16:24,550 --> 01:16:25,698
Doraemon, let's go!

854
01:16:25,698 --> 01:16:27,698
We need to hurry and find the others.

855
01:16:27,698 --> 01:16:28,298
Yup!

856
01:16:28,500 --> 01:16:29,250
Come on.

857
01:17:18,648 --> 01:17:20,348
They're approaching the third entrance.

858
01:17:20,349 --> 01:17:21,349
Shall we capture them?

859
01:17:21,349 --> 01:17:23,298
Don't interfere with anything.

860
01:17:23,298 --> 01:17:24,298
Mister,

861
01:17:24,698 --> 01:17:27,448
Let us show you a grand show.

862
01:18:17,100 --> 01:18:19,300
This door doesn't open at all.

863
01:18:21,449 --> 01:18:23,649
The Slip-Through-Hoop.

864
01:18:35,349 --> 01:18:38,548
Let us goooo!!!

865
01:18:48,449 --> 01:18:49,250
Okay

866
01:18:49,250 --> 01:18:51,250
Lure them to the competition room.

867
01:19:07,598 --> 01:19:10,298
Help us!!

868
01:19:10,500 --> 01:19:11,300
This way!

869
01:19:15,550 --> 01:19:17,800
Mister, shall we get going?

870
01:19:18,100 --> 01:19:18,900
Yeah.

871
01:19:37,298 --> 01:19:40,899
Oh, have found an abnormal engine
wave in the Cretaceous Period.

872
01:19:40,899 --> 01:19:42,199
It seems it's human made.

873
01:19:42,199 --> 01:19:42,750
Okay.

874
01:19:43,550 --> 01:19:44,899
Send in a scout.

875
01:19:44,899 --> 01:19:47,449
I'm certain it's those unofficial hunters.

876
01:19:48,149 --> 01:19:50,500
Time Patrol, number One. Deploy.

877
01:20:00,449 --> 01:20:02,899
Help us!

878
01:20:02,899 --> 01:20:04,149
Help us!!
That's Giant's voice.

879
01:20:04,149 --> 01:20:05,449
Help us!!

880
01:20:05,500 --> 01:20:07,298
Help us !!
Doraemo~n!

881
01:20:07,298 --> 01:20:07,899
Suneo's voice too.

882
01:20:08,000 --> 01:20:08,698
This way!

883
01:20:08,698 --> 01:20:09,448
Yeah.

884
01:20:29,899 --> 01:20:30,699
Shizuka-chan!

885
01:20:31,149 --> 01:20:34,449
Help us, Doraemo~n!

886
01:20:40,399 --> 01:20:41,048
What?!

887
01:20:41,050 --> 01:20:42,449
Welcome.

888
01:20:45,399 --> 01:20:47,899
Welcome to my sports arena.

889
01:20:48,449 --> 01:20:53,050
I built this so that we can watch
dinosaurs fight each other.

890
01:20:53,050 --> 01:20:57,000
Listen, can't you hear the blood-thirsty
dinosaurs all worked up?

891
01:21:10,899 --> 01:21:13,399
The dinosaur will attack
you within five minutes.

892
01:21:13,399 --> 01:21:16,298
If you want me to stop it, hand
over P-suke immediately.

893
01:21:21,550 --> 01:21:23,298
Your time limit is five minutes.

894
01:21:23,298 --> 01:21:24,849
Think it over.

895
01:22:20,850 --> 01:22:22,899
We can't.

896
01:22:22,899 --> 01:22:25,799
I don't care about that long-necked
dinosaur anymore.

897
01:22:26,899 --> 01:22:30,199
This is more interesting. Let's
watch things from here,

898
01:22:35,800 --> 01:22:37,650
Hirari Manteau.

899
01:23:04,250 --> 01:23:05,149
I see...

900
01:23:05,149 --> 01:23:07,750
You're the one that ate the
Kibidango the other day.

901
01:23:10,550 --> 01:23:13,000
Wha-what? That useless fool!

902
01:23:13,000 --> 01:23:15,100
The piece of crap dinosaur!

903
01:23:16,349 --> 01:23:20,748
Yoshi! Let's beat them!

904
01:23:23,100 --> 01:23:24,150
There he is...

905
01:23:30,349 --> 01:23:30,599
A

906
01:23:40,500 --> 01:23:41,300
They're coming!

907
01:23:43,349 --> 01:23:44,298
Run!

908
01:24:07,850 --> 01:24:09,600
Hirari Manteau.

909
01:24:12,949 --> 01:24:13,899
Hirari~.

910
01:24:17,349 --> 01:24:18,548
Hirari.

911
01:24:39,050 --> 01:24:39,899
Wha-what?!

912
01:24:39,899 --> 01:24:42,049
We're the time patrolers. Give yourselves up!

913
01:24:42,050 --> 01:24:43,949
This is the end of your hunting game.

914
01:24:43,949 --> 01:24:47,699
We shall escort you to the twenty-third
century's prison.

915
01:24:48,399 --> 01:24:49,699
Give it up.

916
01:25:11,500 --> 01:25:13,449
Isn't this good, P-suke?

917
01:25:41,750 --> 01:25:42,750
The time...

918
01:25:42,949 --> 01:25:45,849
For P-suke and I to depart has come.

919
01:25:52,500 --> 01:25:54,300
This is your home.

920
01:25:54,500 --> 01:25:55,350
Take care.

921
01:25:57,648 --> 01:25:58,748
P-suke,

922
01:25:59,050 --> 01:26:02,100
Why do you think that we tried
so hard to get you here?

923
01:26:04,698 --> 01:26:06,898
Just listen to me already.

924
01:26:07,899 --> 01:26:09,500
If not, I'm going to hit you.

925
01:26:14,000 --> 01:26:15,899
P-suke!

926
01:26:19,399 --> 01:26:21,949
P-suke! P-suke...

927
01:26:42,298 --> 01:26:43,198
Saito-san...

928
01:26:43,199 --> 01:26:44,649
Let's go while we can.

929
01:26:44,949 --> 01:26:46,849
You sure? Well that's too bad.

930
01:26:46,850 --> 01:26:48,500
Yay, we get to go home.

931
01:26:50,199 --> 01:26:52,099
P-suke, take care.

932
01:26:53,800 --> 01:26:56,500
Our target, Twentieth century,
Tokyo, Nobi residence.

933
01:26:56,500 --> 01:26:57,449
Take off!

934
01:27:14,750 --> 01:27:16,300
Good bye P-suke.

935
01:27:17,149 --> 01:27:19,299
Promise you'll be happy~!

936
01:27:28,550 --> 01:27:31,050
Good bye-!

937
01:28:15,648 --> 01:28:17,448
Ojamashimasu.

938
01:28:17,449 --> 01:28:18,500
What were you all doing upstairs?
Nothing much.

939
01:28:18,500 --> 01:28:19,199
Nothing much.

940
01:28:25,399 --> 01:28:27,298
Well then Nobita-kun. See you later.

941
01:28:27,298 --> 01:28:27,748
Yeah.

942
01:28:27,750 --> 01:28:28,899
See ya!

943
01:28:29,698 --> 01:28:32,048
Suneo, show me your homework, okay?

944
01:28:32,050 --> 01:28:33,050
Sure.

945
01:28:33,050 --> 01:28:35,050
We experienced life and
death together after all.

946
01:28:57,298 --> 01:28:59,498
Good night.

947
01:29:44,550 --> 01:29:46,000
P-suke...

948
01:30:28,100 --> 01:30:31,698
J'm here

949
01:30:31,698 --> 01:30:34,898
Inside your pocket

950
01:30:35,500 --> 01:30:39,000
Together with you

951
01:30:39,149 --> 01:30:42,299
To accompany you on your travels

952
01:30:42,850 --> 01:30:45,200
J've been waiting

953
01:30:46,598 --> 01:30:49,398
Till you realized

954
01:30:50,298 --> 01:30:53,698
The dream you have dreamt

955
01:30:54,000 --> 01:30:57,399
What could it be?

956
01:30:57,899 --> 01:31:01,500
Let's go there right now together

957
01:31:01,698 --> 01:31:06,698
Jt's a world that's distant yet close

958
01:31:07,298 --> 01:31:10,698
Even in my pocket

959
01:31:11,000 --> 01:31:14,300
There's an expansive sky

960
01:31:14,698 --> 01:31:18,298
Even in my pocket

961
01:31:18,449 --> 01:31:21,899
The clouds drift by

962
01:31:22,250 --> 01:31:29,100
There's a wonderful world like this

963
01:31:29,550 --> 01:31:36,600
A world that we travel

964
01:31:37,100 --> 01:31:40,300
Even in my pocket

965
01:31:40,750 --> 01:31:44,050
There's a vast ocean

966
01:31:44,500 --> 01:31:47,699
Even in my pocket

967
01:31:48,199 --> 01:31:51,399
Birds take flight

968
01:31:51,899 --> 01:31:58,799
There's a wonderful world like this

969
01:31:59,349 --> 01:32:06,298
A world that we travel

